    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d225">

                <pb facs="0382" n="290" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v01/pg290"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/10742</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Switzerland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Stovall</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Berne</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-07-18T13:00:00+01:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">July 18, 1918, 1 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received July 20, 3.16 a.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3997. My 3914, July 9.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d225-f1"/> I learn that memorandum
                    mentioned was later submitted by my Bulgarian informant to British official,
                    Geneva, who is taking up with his Government the question of giving financial
                    support to Bulgarian Revolutionary Party. Efforts are also being made to
                    facilitate the journey to Switzerland of Bulgarian <pb facs="0383" n="291"
                        xml:id="pg291"/> Radical leader … to ascertain his plans and possibility of
                    such a revolutionary movement.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stovall</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
